The paper’s native witness is exactly a 2-coloring of the vertices whose two induced subgraphs have maximum degree at most two and no cycle. The decisive caveats are also explicit: maximum degree ≤4 is essentially trivial, bounded treewidth is FPT (Theorem 4.2), and Section 5 gives an \(O(n^2)\)-variable SAT/ILP formulation. So any viable Track A generator must use degree-5, growing-treewidth graphs and must actually defeat a Section-5-style constraint solver; worst-case NP-hardness alone will not be enough.
